

The function cpsw_ndo_start_xmit is called to perform the low-level transmission operations (such as padding, timestamping, and submitting to DMA) when the packet is ready to be transmitted via the CPSW (Crossbar Switch) network interface.

After the dev_queue xmit() fucntion the ndo_xmit_function is called.

IN SHORT WHAT HAPPENS : 

		Padding: The packet is padded to meet the minimum size requirement if necessary (skb_padto()).

		Timestamping: If hardware timestamping is enabled and supported, the timestamp flag is set.

		Queue Selection: The appropriate transmit queue is chosen based on the packet’s metadata (skb_get_queue_mapping()).
						using the cpu affinity.

		Channel Selection: The appropriate DMA channel is selected based on the queue index.

		Packet Submission: The packet is then submitted to the DMA for actual transmission using cpdma_chan_submit(). This step interacts with
		 the hardware to send the packet over the network.
		 


